<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Judaism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jewish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Judaism is the monotheistic religion of the Jewish people, based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> and rabbinic tradition. Its history was shaped by the Assyrian and Chaldean conquests, the Achaemenid restoration and the conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> elite adopted Judaism, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> became a major centre of Jewish life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/judaism.jpg" alt="Judaism" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ariely · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Menorah_0307.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
